WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.680
Why does Romans end with so many names?

2
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.600
After chapters about sin, grace,

3
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.600
and life in Christ, Paul greets people.

4
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.500
Phoebe had helped many.

5
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.760
Prisca and Aquila had risked their lives for him.

6
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.200
Mary had worked hard for the church.

7
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.840
Those greetings show us the people living out the gospel.

8
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.800
They opened homes, served, and cared for one another.

9
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.500
Names matter because people matter.

10
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.620
That makes me pay closer attention

11
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.040
to the people around me:

12
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.880
the person who encourages me,

13
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.360
opens a home, or quietly serves.

14
00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.500
As you read Romans sixteen,

15
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.100
pause over the names.

16
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:42.820
Then remember someone

17
00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.520
whose faithfulness has helped you,

18
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:45.620
and thank them.
